sequenceDiagram
    title Execution flow — Runtime + Platform cadence (precise Rust facade signatures)

    participant Caller as Caller<br/>::session_v4::CompilerSession::eval (REPL trailing expr) or ::main (Run mode trampoline)
    participant Trampoline as Trampoline<br/>::session_v4::CompilerSession::trampoline
    participant IoObs as IoObserver<br/>cranelisp_intrinsics::register_io_observer<br/>(extension point — consumer state in src::io_trace)

    Note over Caller, IoObs: † marks proposed/target API not yet in current code.<br/>Receiver is implicit in the lifeline.<br/>Runtime cadence begins when JIT'd user code starts executing — ends when the trampoline returns to the caller.<br/>Per Decision 43 the running-program substrate is split across cranelisp-primitives (user-callable) and cranelisp-intrinsics (backend-emitted-call targets shown below).<br/>Compilation internals (typecheck, codegen) delegated to exec-flow-compilation.<br/>IoObserver registration (extension point per facades/intrinsics.md §"IO observation") happens once at session init from int when REPL/trace mode or CRANELISP_IO_TRACE=1 is active. Production batch: no observer registered, one relaxed null-check load per emit site.

    rect rgb(245, 230, 255)
        Note over Caller, Trampoline: ENTRY — caller invokes the trampoline with a code pointer + expected type<br/>(code_ptr was obtained from ST[m].get(sym).code.ptr() or from a per-eval JITModule)

        Caller ->> Trampoline: CompilerSession::trampoline(code_ptr: *const u8, expected_type: &Type) -> Result<EvalValue, RuntimeError>
        Note over Trampoline: classify expected_type —<br/>if non-IO (Int / Bool / String / Float / ADT / Fn / etc.) — direct call, return value<br/>if IO inner_type — direct call to build the IO tree, then walk via run_io_trampoline
    end

    rect rgb(220, 235, 255)
        Note over Trampoline: USER CODE EXECUTION — Trampoline calls JIT'd code via raw fn pointer<br/>UserCode runs with RC, GOT, and (potentially) cross-module dispatch interleaved

        create participant UserCode as User code<br/>(JIT'd Cranelift output — registered via JITBuilder::symbol_lookup_fn pointing into the SymbolTable GOT, per Decision 23)
        Trampoline ->> UserCode: indirect call via fn pointer — args per Type signature, abi=SystemV

        opt heap allocation needed (string literal, ADT constructor, closure capture, Vec push, etc.)
            create participant Allocator as Heap allocator<br/>cranelisp_intrinsics::alloc (per Decision 43 — backend-emitted-call target)
            UserCode ->> Allocator: cranelisp_intrinsics::heap_alloc(payload_size: i64) -> i64
            Note over Allocator: layout — [total_size: u64 | rc: u64 | payload bytes...]<br/>returns base pointer (offset 0) — payload starts at offset 16. Per src/CLAUDE.md "Heap Access".
            Allocator -->> UserCode: ptr: i64 (base of allocation)
        end

        opt RC inc on shared use (consuming convention — caller inc's non-last-use heap args before passing)
            Note over UserCode: inline atomic_rmw add 1, Ordering::Relaxed on rc field at ptr+8 —<br/>NO runtime call. Backend emits the atomic instruction directly.
        end

        opt RC dec on scope exit (consuming convention — callee owns heap params, dec's at scope exit)
            Note over UserCode: inline atomic_rmw sub 1, Ordering::Release on rc field —<br/>NO runtime call. Backend emits the atomic instruction directly.
            opt old_rc == 1 (last reference — must drop)
                Note over UserCode: inline Acquire fence, then call per-type drop_glue
                create participant DropGlue as Per-type drop_glue<br/>(JIT'd by cranelisp_backend per ADT / closure / Vec layout — embedded code_ptr in closure header per Decision 11)
                UserCode ->> DropGlue: drop_glue(ptr: i64) — recursively dec heap-typed fields, then dealloc outer
                opt nested heap fields
                    DropGlue ->> DropGlue: recursive dec on each heap field (may invoke other drop_glues via the same fn-ptr mechanism)
                end
                DropGlue ->> Allocator: cranelisp_intrinsics::heap_dealloc(ptr: i64)
                Note over Allocator: reads total_size from ptr+0 — frees the full allocation back to the system allocator
            end
        end

        opt cross-module call (callee resides in a different module — m2/foo)
            create participant GOT as GOT[m2]<br/>cranelisp_types::module::GotTable (Arc<GotTable> field on SymbolTable[m2])
            Note over UserCode, GOT: call site emitted as global_value against __cranelisp_got_m2 + slot offset, then atomic_load, then indirect call (per Decision 23)
            UserCode ->> GOT: GotTable::load_slot(slot: usize) -> *const u8 (atomic_load, Ordering::Acquire)
            GOT -->> UserCode: code_ptr — current function address for m2/foo
            UserCode ->> UserCode: indirect call through code_ptr (transparent cross-module dispatch — REPL redefinition retargets via atomic GOT-slot store, per Decision 31)
        end
    end

    alt expected_type is non-IO — UserCode returns the value directly
        UserCode -->> Trampoline: i64 (value bits — per Type repr)
        Trampoline -->> Caller: Ok(EvalValue { repr: i64, ty: Type, heap_root: Option<Arc<HeapRetention>> }) †
    else expected_type is IO inner_type — UserCode returns an IO tree pointer
        UserCode -->> Trampoline: io_root_ptr: i64 (heap-allocated IO node — Pure | Effect | Bind | Par)

        rect rgb(220, 255, 220)
            Note over Trampoline: IO WALK — trampoline reduces the IO tree to a final value via run_io_trampoline

            create participant IORuntime as IO trampoline<br/>cranelisp_intrinsics::io (per Decision 43 — backend-emitted-call target)
            Trampoline ->> IORuntime: cranelisp_intrinsics::cranelisp_run_io(io_root_ptr: i64) -> i64
            Note over IORuntime: reduces the IO tree node-by-node, consuming each outer allocation via rc::dec_shallow_io (per Decision 29)
            opt IoObserver registered (relaxed-load null check)
                Note over IORuntime, IoObs: extension-point emit on trampoline entry — facades/intrinsics.md §"IO observation"
                IORuntime ->> IoObs: IoObserver(IoEventTag::TrampolineEnter, &IoEvent { /* root payload */ })
            end

            loop walk IO tree until fully reduced
                alt current node is Pure(value)
                    Note over IORuntime: load value from payload — return value from this branch
                    opt IoObserver registered
                        IORuntime ->> IoObs: IoObserver(IoEventTag::PureStep, &IoEvent { /* value */ })
                    end
                else current node is Effect(fq: FQSymbol, args, continuation)
                    Note over IORuntime: dispatch the effect via direct GOT lookup per Decision 26 — NO HostContext::dispatch wrapper (facades/platform.md §2.13).<br/>IORuntime reads got_slot off the resolved ModuleEntry::Def for fq's PrimitiveKind::PlatformEffect entry (S66 post-rollback — GOT is the single source of truth for callable addresses), and scheduling_class from the same variant.

                    create participant ST_fq as ST[fq.module]<br/>SymbolTable [generic C=Code, L=()]<br/>(reached via Sess.shared.symbol_tables.get(&fq.module))
                    IORuntime ->> ST_fq: SymbolTable::get(&fq.symbol) -> Option[Ref[ModuleEntry[Code]]]
                    ST_fq -->> IORuntime: Some(Ref[ModuleEntry::Def { got_slot: Some(slot), kind: DefKind::Primitive { primitive_kind: PrimitiveKind::PlatformEffect { scheduling_class } }, .. }])
                    IORuntime ->> ST_fq: SymbolTable::got.load_slot(slot)
                    ST_fq -->> IORuntime: ptr (the platform DLL fn address, Acquire ordering)
                    Note over IORuntime: marshal args via CLType::from_repr (CLInt / CLString / CLBool / CLFloat / CLIO _)
                    create participant PlatformDLL as Platform DLL<br/>(loaded via cranelisp_platform::load_manifest from {project_root}/platforms/{name}.dylib — example: stdio.<br/>Per Decision 26 (S66 amendment plus rollback) the per-symbol GOT slot — read via SymbolTable.got.load_slot(slot) — is the runtime call target.)
                    IORuntime ->> PlatformDLL: indirect call via ptr from the GOT (declared by the platform's declare_platform! macro, exported with derive_jit_name)
                    Note over PlatformDLL: platform fn body runs — may call back into runtime via HostCallbacks for alloc / dec / rc_inc / invoke_closure (callbacks installed once per session by HostContext::init at CompilerSession::new)
                    opt platform fn needs to allocate (e.g. produce a CLString result)
                        PlatformDLL ->> Allocator: HostCallbacks.alloc(size: usize) -> *mut u8
                        Note over Allocator: callback routes to cranelisp_intrinsics::heap_alloc — same allocator as user code, same RC discipline
                        Allocator -->> PlatformDLL: ptr
                    end
                    PlatformDLL -->> IORuntime: CLType repr (i64) — return value of the platform fn
                    opt IoObserver registered
                        IORuntime ->> IoObs: IoObserver(IoEventTag::PlatformEffect, &IoEvent { /* fq, args, result */ })
                    end
                    Note over IORuntime: continue the walk with continuation(value) — pop continuation frame from cont_stack
                    opt IoObserver registered (continuation pop)
                        IORuntime ->> IoObs: IoObserver(IoEventTag::ContPop, &IoEvent { /* … */ })
                    end
                else current node is Bind(io_lhs, continuation_closure)
                    Note over IORuntime: recursively reduce io_lhs, then call continuation_closure(lhs_result) which produces another IO node — push onto cont_stack
                    opt IoObserver registered
                        IORuntime ->> IoObs: IoObserver(IoEventTag::Bind, &IoEvent { /* … */ })
                    end
                else current node is Par(io_branches)
                    Note over IORuntime: fork-join via rayon — each branch reduced concurrently — collect results when all branches complete
                    opt IoObserver registered
                        IORuntime ->> IoObs: IoObserver(IoEventTag::Par, &IoEvent { /* branch count */ })
                    end
                end
            end

            IORuntime -->> Trampoline: i64 (final reduced value — per inner_type repr)
        end

        Trampoline -->> Caller: Ok(EvalValue { repr: i64, ty: inner_type, heap_root: Option<Arc<HeapRetention>> }) †
    end

    Note over Caller: EvalValue.heap_root keeps any returned heap allocation alive until the caller drops the value —<br/>see exec-flow-repl Display formatting (the formatter reads through the value and may recurse into nested heap structures).
